# Shell scripts and bats tests MUST check out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Git Bash runs the tokenwar scripts on Windows. A checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# (the Git for Windows default) rewrites them to CRLF, and a trailing \r then breaks
# the shebang line, `case` patterns, and every `[[ "$x" == "literal" ]]` comparison.
# Declaring eol=lf here makes the checkout correct regardless of the user's config.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bats      text eol=lf
install.sh  text eol=lf
uninstall.sh text eol=lf

# Windows-side entry points are consumed by cmd.exe / PowerShell, which want CRLF.
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf

# Everything else: let Git normalise text, leave binaries alone.
*.md        text
*.json      text
*.yml       text
*.html      text
*.png       binary
